      "id": 7679,
      "name": "Ironic",
      "username": "Ironic",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-13T07:38:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>They're the same person, right? &nbsp;All the other sets give each other buffs, these ones take each other out of play. &nbsp;They look identical, right down to the outfit (and not only do the Citizens not have a stock uniform, almost all of them except Truth/Dare and Dawn herself just wear street clothes). &nbsp;The flavor texts are so dramatically opposed, it seems like a split personality, though I suppose it might just be a powerful minion with a wide range of powers being shown as two cards to get a better range of their abilities.</p><p>Ironic</p><p>P.S. Also, unless I'm wrong, Truth/Dare is the only non-Character villain to appear on Chrono-Ranger's Bounty cards. &nbsp;The mechanical reference is clear (that Bounty is useless against Characters, and specifically hoses Trash-based Villains such as Dawn), but I wonder if it also means that he's a particularly powerful or plot-relevant minion.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:01.044Z",
